  {
   "uuid": "ef87a7b2-3e0e-4705-9f59-a1cb2bd0938f",
   "text": "",
   "content": [
    {
     "start_timestamp": "2025-12-07T23:30:02.000000Z",
     "stop_timestamp": "2025-12-07T23:30:14.454000Z",
     "type": "text",
     "text": "**Turkey & bean chili (5 big servings)**\n\nIngredients\n- 2 lb (900 g) 93% lean ground turkey\n- 2 cans (15 oz) black beans, drained and rinsed\n- 1 can (15 oz) kidney beans, drained and rinsed\n- 1 can (28 oz) crushed tomatoes\n- 1 can (15 oz) diced tomatoes\n- 1 large onion, diced\n- 1 red bell pepper, diced\n- 4 cloves garlic, minced\n- 2 tbsp chili powder, 1 tbsp cumin, 1 tsp smoked paprika, 1 tsp oregano\n- 1 tbsp tomato paste\n- 1 cup chicken broth\n- salt, pepper, 1 tbsp oil\n\nSteps\n1. Heat oil in the Dutch oven, cook onion and pepper 5–6 min.\n2. Add garlic, tomato paste and spices, stir 1 min.\n3. Add turkey, break it up, cook until no longer pink (~8 min).\n4. Add tomatoes, beans, broth. Simmer partly covered 45 min, stirring now and then.\n5. Salt to taste. Cool, split into 5 containers.\n\nRough macros per serving\n- ~520 kcal\n- ~48 g protein\n- ~45 g carbs (~15 g fiber)\n- ~15 g fat\n\nCost is roughly $18–24 total depending on the turkey, so about $4–5 per lunch.",
     "citations": []
    }
   ],
   "sender": "assistant",
